    "description": "## Objective\n\nDeliver all access through Permission Sets and Permission Set Groups across four tiers: Rep, Manager, Ops, Admin. No profile-based access.\n\n## Implementation Requirements\n\n* Permission Set Groups: WT_Rep_PSG, WT_Manager_PSG, WT_Ops_PSG, WT_Admin_PSG\n* Component permission sets: WT_Reference_Data_Read, WT_Reference_Data_Admin, WT_SignUp_Logging, WT_Proof_Upload, WT_Deal_Config, WT_Assignment_Mgmt, WT_SignUp_Review_Override, WT_Integration\n* Role hierarchy and org-wide defaults per design doc story A-03\n* Object/field access per the Permissions section of each object story\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n* Login-as checks pass per tier: rep sees own records only, manager sees team, Ops can override and reassign, integration user has least-privilege create/update\n\n## Testing Notes\n\nLogin-as matrix across all four tiers.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nLicense type changes (deferred to renewal).\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n* PS/PSG-only access is what makes the future Platform Plus license switch a non-event.\n\n---\n\nEstimate: L · \\~24h · Dependencies: POC object stories · Ticket BUILD-01 (approved 2026-07-04)",
